{mi do dunda be ko'a}:

[1(2[dunda1 (give-r(s)) :] mi I, me)2 (3[dunda3 (recipient(s)) :] do=20
you)3 [is, does] =AB4{5dunda giv-ing be (6[dunda2 (gift(s)) :] ko'a=20
he/she/it)6}5=BB4]1

Clearly, someone must have implemented it this way (knowingly, I=20
assume). Of course, we cannot be sure that jbofi'e has any authority=20
about such things. The most useful interpretation should optimally be=20
the preferred one.

Here is a past thread on this very topic:=20
https://groups.google.com/forum/#!msg/lojban-beginners/QiZ5pF9q34I/MDaYSI0q=
0agJ

